-- title:
--   Monogenicity of a finite extension of discrete valuation rings
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, and let $B$ likewise be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, equipped with the structure of an $A$-algebra. Assume that the structure map $A \to B$ is a local homomorphism, i.e. it pulls the maximal ideal of $B$ back into the maximal ideal of $A$, that $B$ is a finite (finitely generated) module over $A$, and that the induced extension of residue fields $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A) \to \mathrm{ResidueField}(B)$ is separable as an algebra extension. Assume further, as an explicit hypothesis, that the structure map $A \to B$ is injective. Then there exists an element $x \in B$ such that the $A$-subalgebra of $B$ generated by the singleton $\{x\}$ is the whole of $B$; that is, $B = A[x]$ for a single element $x$. Note that only the existence of such a generator is asserted: no control on $x$ (for instance via its image in the residue field, or its valuation) is part of the conclusion.
--
--   This is the classical monogenicity statement for a finite local extension of discrete valuation rings with separable residue extension (Serre, Corps locaux, Ch. III, §6, Prop. 12). It is the hypothesis under which ramification invariants may be computed from a single generator, and within this development it feeds the computations of lower ramification groups, of the different, and of fixed subrings used there.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_exists_adjoin_singleton_eq_top_of_isSeparable_residueField.lean

